# ensuring that the author list and other fields remain accurate.

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Introduction to Agentic Coding
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Chris
    family-names: Endemann
    email: endemann@wisc.edu
  - given-names: Tracy
    family-names: Reuter
  - given-names: Tejvir
    family-names: Mann
abstract: >-
  A Carpentries-style lesson on working effectively and
  safely with AI coding agents as a researcher. Covers the
  agentic tooling landscape, security and credential
  hygiene, supply-chain and provider trust, repository
  reconnaissance, specification and feature-driven
  development, verification and review of agent-generated
  analyses, and cost, context, and energy management.
  Developed from the "Agentic Coding Best Practices"
  workshop at the UW-Madison ML Marathon.
license: CC-BY-4.0
